snapshot: skip crafted . and .. tree entries, fixes F-015

From: Andy Green <andy@warmcat.com>

Archive member names were taken verbatim from tree entries, so a
pusher using plumbing could plant directory entries named .. that
accumulated into path-traversal members (tar-slip on extraction by
tools that honor them literally).  Skip entries named . or .. during
the walk, closing the crafted-object route.
---
 lib/job/snapshot.c |   18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/job/snapshot.c b/lib/job/snapshot.c
index 9c89fdd..66b7ee2 100644
--- a/lib/job/snapshot.c
+++ b/lib/job/snapshot.c
@@ -499,6 +499,24 @@ job_snapshot(struct jg2_ctx *ctx)
 			continue;
 		}
 
+		/*
+		 * Crafted tree objects (plumbing push without fsck) can name
+		 * entries "." or ".."; walked verbatim these accumulate into
+		 * archive members that escape the extraction dir (tar-slip).
+		 * Git clients refuse to create them, so just skip them.
+		 */
+		{
+			const char *ten = git_tree_entry_name(te);
+
+			if (!strcmp(ten, ".") || !strcmp(ten, "..")) {
+				lwsl_notice("%s: skipping hostile entry "
+					    "\"%s\" in snapshot walk\n",
+					    __func__, ten);
+
+				continue;
+			}
+		}
+
 		switch (git_tree_entry_type(te)) {
 
 		case GIT_OBJ_TREE:
